@page "/"

<PageTitle>About</PageTitle>

<h1> About the Game </h1>
<p>
    Your goal is to collect powerups to grow longer, obtaining the highest score possible.
    Be aware of obstacles in the world, such as walls and other snake players. Collide with one of these objects and it's game over!
</p>

<h1> Features </h1>
<ul>
    <li><b> Movement Controls: </b> Use the standard WASD to control the snake through the world. </li>
    <li><b> Snake Growth & Power-Ups: </b> Control a snake that grows longer by collecting power-ups (food) scattered throughout the world. </li>
    <li><b> Collisions & Respawn: </b> Colliding with walls and other snakes results in death. Respawn will happen at a random location a few moments after death. </li>
    <li><b> Connecting & Disconnecting: </b> Connect to the game with an address and port of your choosing. To start a new instance of the game, simply use the disconnect button, enter your player information, and click on connect. </li>
    <li><b> Easier Reconnecting: </b> This client offers the ability to reconnect without restarting the web browser or refreshing the page. </li>
    <li><b> Stylized Powerups: </b> The powerups are a bunch of exotic tropical fruits instead of boring colored dots. </li>
    <li><b> Stylized Deaths: </b> The head of the snake will explode whenever a snake dies. </li>
</ul>

<h1> Design Choices </h1>
<ul>
    <li>
        <b> Game Loop: </b>
        When the client first pulls up the webpage, the game loop is immediately called.
        This is to guarantee that the game loop will be already established and filling with information as the client enters it.
        To verify that the game loop does not start running before it has all needed information, multiple checks are put in place to verify that all data is loaded before drawing.
    </li>
    <li>
        <b> Connection Errors: </b>
        Connection errors can occur when a player enters the incorrect address or port, attempts to connect to an inactive server, or if any issue occurs during connection.
        Whenever any of these issues occur, a popup is displayed indicating that a connection error occurred.
        The popup will remain until the client retries connection, where the error box with either disappear permanently or reappear upon another issue occurring.
        This design was chosen so that the reason for disconnection could be displayed until the player was able to correct it.
    </li>
    <li>
        <b> Player Name Errors: </b>
        Player name errors can occur when a player enters an invalid name. An invalid name is considered one that is less than 1 character and greater than 16 characters.
        The error box remains on screen until the player enters a valid snake name, as the popup contains information regarding name specifications.
        As soon as a valid name is entered, the error message will disappear.
    </li>
</ul>

<h1> What Works and What Doesn't </h1>
<ul>
    <li>
        <b> Overview: </b> 
        From thorough testing of this assignment, it appears that all necessary features function without error.
        In certain circumstances, such as disconnecting or clicking onto another page, the program will throw an exception.
        All exceptions have been modified to be gracefully handled based on the code that threw it.
    </li>
</ul>

